{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788263985,"nonce":"2pBqqaKi5Ixd5UipvkcgGD1L9N0=","title":"--quicktest and autostart.rws race: restoring the save deterministically breaks the bench fixture","message":"Playbook lesson `[[quicktest-and-autostart-collide]]` was written during M1 run `m1-20260831` and has never had an issue. Filing it, because the standing bench-hygiene decision it forces is not a note — it is a fixture contract, and right now the bench works only because a file is parked in a directory with nothing explaining why.\n\n## The collision\n\n`autostart.rws` is currently parked in `Saves/pre-m1/` alongside the five pre-run autosaves. **Restoring it to `Saves/` re-breaks `--quicktest` deterministically.**\n\nRoot cause, from the lesson: `Root_Entry` and `Root_Play` race on `Root.checkedAutostartSaveFile` with a scene-targeted long event. Two launches during M1 failed on this before the third succeeded; both Player.logs were captured and are archived at `RUNS/m1-20260831/mapgen-failure-{1,2}.Player.log`.\n\n## Why it needs a decision rather than a note\n\nThe bench fixture is `run-agent.sh --quicktest`. Whether an `autostart.rws` may exist in `Saves/` is therefore part of the fixture, not a preference — and the current state is a file moved out of the way by hand, in a directory whose name records the move but not the reason. The next person to restore the save gets two failed launches and no explanation, exactly as session 12 did.\n\nThere are two coherent answers and they are mutually exclusive:\n\n1. **Leave `autostart.rws` parked, and say so in the bench docs** — `profile/` and the bench README get a stated rule that `Saves/autostart.rws` must not exist while `--quicktest` is the fixture, with the `Root.checkedAutostartSaveFile` race cited as the reason.\n2. **Restore `autostart.rws` and retire `--quicktest`** — the fixture becomes the save, which is more reproducible (a fixed map rather than a fresh random tile) but changes what every acceptance run is measuring, and 4.3's temperate-fixture requirement would then be satisfied by construction rather than by draw.\n\nThis is a policy call, not a mechanism one — the mechanism is already root-caused. Evan's, or the orchestrator's under a stated rationale.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- One of the two options above is chosen, implemented, and the reasoning recorded in DESIGN.md's decisions log.\n- The bench docs state the rule explicitly, with the `Root.checkedAutostartSaveFile` citation, so a future session cannot recreate the collision by tidying.\n- `[[quicktest-and-autostart-collide]]` is cited from wherever a session would actually read it before launching (`playbook/SESSION-START.md` position, or the bench script's own header).\n- If option 2 is chosen: every acceptance suite that assumes a fresh map is re-checked against a fixed one before the switch lands.","files":null}]}